# Entries a fresh `brew bundle dump` does not produce on this machine.
# scripts/capture appends this file to the dump and drops any line the dump
# already covers, so everything recorded here survives a re-capture.
#
# Two reasons an entry belongs here:
#   1. The dump aborts its dependency sort on a libtiff/webp cycle in the
#      installed keg tabs, and silently omits whatever it had not reached.
#   2. `mas` is not installed, so the dump reports no App Store apps at all.
#      It is listed below and will be present after the first bootstrap.

# Verified installed with `brew list`, absent from the dump.
brew "go"

# Wanted on a new Mac, installed here outside Homebrew.
brew "mas"
cask "kitty"
cask "mactex-no-gui"

# Mac App Store apps. scripts/capture refreshes these once `mas` is installed.
mas "AdBlock", id: 1402042596
